nd you just bring her back to  normal  [Music]  [Music]  one of the most awesome ass kicking this  2020 courtesy of one piece comes in the  form of  zorro vs camazo it's a brutal showdown  between multi-wielders that gave us some  of the best fight animations and  adaptations in this year for one piece  the anime did some retouching on this  scene which drew quite the divisive  reception from the fan base that  compared it to the manga nonetheless you  can't deny that the effects did add  quite a bit to the fight which is  already an amazing display of zorro's  prowess  catching up to one piece is a ginormous  task but now you know what's in store  the animation in the wano arc has been  pretty spot-on there's a reason why the  series is still one of the biggest ones  worldwide and while i don't think that  the fights are the primary reasons for  that  they sure play a decently major part  [Music]  sao's final alicization season had its  moments with its fights  and while i enjoyed a lot of them i  think that it would be a shame not to  include the finale on a top 10 list  on the first list i gave the nod to the  berkoli fight for the sheer awesomeness  of the cool uncle mentor character being  badass and it's breathtaking animation  however on a personal basis  this is the fight that i go back to once  in a while to re-watch  kirito versus sometimes is probably one  of the best finales a fan of the series  can ask for we get to see kirito firing  off the  culmination of all his experiences and  skills obtained in underworld as well as  updated callbacks to when the series was  the hottest thing in town  like the starburst dream while in his  signature old attire and don't tell me  you don't get a little bit emotional  when kirito took the thoughts and  prayers of every single living being in  underworld in the form of stars to  unleash his final attack  i think the one thing that seriously  holds this fight back is the lack of a  connection between the two combatants  they're just fighting each other for the  sake of protecting or destroying this  world and it would have been better  if somtalizer was someone kirito had a  personal stake with  four gil returns with a second fight to  make the list it's really telling when  your anime with less  episodes than one hand can count already  has two fights that i can claim are some  of the top fights in 2020  but fog hill of five elements did it but  today i'm featuring the bridge fight  which is really no slouch compared to  the one i featured on the previous list  if you recall i did feature this one on  yet another list but i think that it  just holds up so well to have it on  multiple lists even when you look at  2020 as a whole i still find this so  exhilarating and the fact that it's on a  show that's not being watched by many is  just the icing on top fog hill is not  a huge time investment so i really  encourage you to give it a try the story  is decent but when it comes to the  animation of fight scenes  it's outright top tier even in 2020 as a  whole  if you want me to name a hidden gem this  year with respect to the anime's overall  popularity and the quality of fight  scenes then hitori noshita would find  its way to the top of the list  it's a serious contender for topping  that list outright if you don't believe  me  let the clip do the talking for me then  to the animator's credit the research  really shows i honestly believe it's one  of the strongest points of the series  the guys doing the animating really know  their stuff in hitori noshita you can  really feel a sense of realism in its  combat scenes just watch and tell me if  you agree with what i see  you can really feel the impact of each  blow here if you consider yourself a  martial arts aficionado you might want  to try hitori no [ __ ] out however i'd  recommend not watching this just for the  fight and starting all the way back in  its first season  danwachi has its fair share of great  fights in its sea